{"person_id":"robert-palmer","name":"Robert Palmer","cohort_group":"Creators / artists","category":"Musician/singer","birth_year":1949,"age_at_milestone":25,"milestone_by_age_26":"Released debut solo album 'Sneakin' Sally Through the Alley' on Island Records in September 1974 at age 25, following three albums with Vinegar Joe on Island Records (1972-1973).","early_history_summary":"Palmer joined his first band at 15 in Scarborough and by 20 had replaced Jess Roden in the Alan Bown Set (1969). He formed Vinegar Joe with Elkie Brooks in 1971, signed to Island Records, and released three albums before going solo in 1974.","primary_leverage_engine":"Vocal talent and early band experience","normalized_primary_engine":"Early specialization / prior reps","secondary_engine":"Island Records platform","started_serious_reps_before_20_score":1,"prior_reps_score":2,"scarce_skill_depth_score":1,"native_distribution_score":1,"elite_ecosystem_network_score":1,"complementary_team_score":1,"structural_wave_score":1,"concentration_intensity_score":1,"capital_safety_score":0,"domain_proximity_score":1,"total_leverage_score":10,"success_tier":2,"leverage_evidence_confidence":"Medium","family_context_summary":"Palmer was born in Batley, Yorkshire, and moved to Malta as an infant where his father worked in British naval intelligence. The family returned to the UK when he was 12, settling in Scarborough.","parent_family_domain_summary":"Not documented in reviewed sources.","early_family_financial_platform_support_score":0,"parent_family_domain_advantage_score":0,"inherited_audience_business_network_score":0,"elite_institution_performance_pipeline_score":1,"frontier_geography_ecosystem_score":1,"rare_early_tools_facilities_score":0,"dedicated_mentor_coach_tutor_score":0,"exceptional_peer_cofounder_sibling_score":1,"early_online_platform_community_score":0,"direct_customer_domain_exposure_score":1,"prodigy_physical_edge_score":0,"adversity_constraint_catalyst_score":0,"inherited_access_stack_count":4,"exceptional_inherited_access_count":0,"all_documented_early_condition_count":4,"primary_early_advantage_archetype":"Self-created domain repetition","primary_early_advantage_tags":"early band experience, vocal versatility, Island Records signing, London music scene, Elkie Brooks collaboration","evidence_summary":"Palmer started performing in bands at age 15 in Scarborough, joining the Mandrakes while still at school. By 20, he had joined the Alan Bown Set, and by 22 formed Vinegar Joe with Elkie Brooks, signing to Island Records and releasing three albums between 1972 and 1973. His debut solo album 'Sneakin' Sally Through the Alley' was released on Island Records in September 1974 at age 25. His early path was built on a decade of performing experience in bands and access to the London music industry through his Island Records deal.","early_advantage_evidence_confidence":"Medium","source_count":4,"primary_source_url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_Palmer_(singer)","source_urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_Palmer_(singer)","https://www.allmusic.com/album/MW0000191222","https://robertpalmer.com/biography/","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vinegar_Joe_(band)"],"annotation_status":"subagent_researched_beta","source_audit_status":"not_independently_audited","data_version":"0.2.0-subagent-beta","eligibility_status":"age_26_eligible"}
{"person_id":"sergio-leone","name":"Sergio Leone","cohort_group":"Creators / artists","category":"Film director","birth_year":1929,"age_at_milestone":26,"milestone_by_age_26":"By age 26 (1955), Leone had worked as assistant director and second unit director on approximately 50 Italian and American films at Cinecittà Studios, including major Hollywood productions Quo Vadis (1951) and Helen of Troy (1955).","early_history_summary":"Leone was the son of cinema pioneer Vincenzo Leone and silent film actress Bice Waleran. He began working in film at 18 as an assistant to Vittorio De Sica on Bicycle Thieves (1948), then spent the 1950s as assistant director and second unit director on dozens of films at Cinecittà, including major Hollywood productions.","primary_leverage_engine":"Family-domain apprenticeship","normalized_primary_engine":"Early specialization / prior reps","secondary_engine":"Cinecittà ecosystem access","started_serious_reps_before_20_score":1,"prior_reps_score":2,"scarce_skill_depth_score":1,"native_distribution_score":0,"elite_ecosystem_network_score":2,"complementary_team_score":0,"structural_wave_score":1,"concentration_intensity_score":1,"capital_safety_score":0,"domain_proximity_score":2,"total_leverage_score":10,"success_tier":1,"leverage_evidence_confidence":"Medium","family_context_summary":"Leone was born in Rome, the son of cinema pioneer Vincenzo Leone (known as Roberto Roberti) and silent film actress Edvige Valcarenghi (Bice Waleran). His father was prevented from working during the 1930s by Italy's Fascist regime.","parent_family_domain_summary":"Both parents were deeply embedded in the Italian film industry: his father was a pioneer film director and his mother was a silent film actress, providing direct domain immersion from childhood.","early_family_financial_platform_support_score":1,"parent_family_domain_advantage_score":2,"inherited_audience_business_network_score":1,"elite_institution_performance_pipeline_score":2,"frontier_geography_ecosystem_score":2,"rare_early_tools_facilities_score":1,"dedicated_mentor_coach_tutor_score":1,"exceptional_peer_cofounder_sibling_score":0,"early_online_platform_community_score":0,"direct_customer_domain_exposure_score":1,"prodigy_physical_edge_score":0,"adversity_constraint_catalyst_score":0,"inherited_access_stack_count":8,"exceptional_inherited_access_count":3,"all_documented_early_condition_count":8,"primary_early_advantage_archetype":"Family-domain apprenticeship","primary_early_advantage_tags":"film industry family, Cinecittà access, Hollywood productions, early industry immersion, De Sica mentorship","evidence_summary":"Leone was born into the Italian film industry as the son of pioneer director Vincenzo Leone and silent film actress Bice Waleran. He began working in film at 18 as an assistant to Vittorio De Sica on Bicycle Thieves (1948). Over the next decade, he worked on approximately 50 Italian and American films as assistant director and second unit director at Cinecittà Studios, including major Hollywood productions like Quo Vadis (1951) and Helen of Troy (1955). His family connections and early immersion in the film industry provided direct domain access from a young age.","early_advantage_evidence_confidence":"High","source_count":4,"primary_source_url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sergio_Leone","source_urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sergio_Leone","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sergio_Leone_filmography","http://www.filmreference.com/Directors-Ku-Lu/Leone-Sergio.html","http://www.sensesofcinema.com/2002/great-directors/leone/"],"annotation_status":"subagent_researched_beta","source_audit_status":"not_independently_audited","data_version":"0.2.0-subagent-beta","eligibility_status":"age_26_eligible"}
{"person_id":"jay-z","name":"Jay-Z","cohort_group":"Creators / artists","category":"Rapper/musician","birth_year":1969,"age_at_milestone":26,"milestone_by_age_26":"Co-founded Roc-A-Fella Records in 1995 (age 25-26) and released debut album 'Reasonable Doubt' on June 25, 1996 (age 26), which peaked at #23 on the Billboard 200.","early_history_summary":"Jay-Z (Shawn Carter) started rapping at 16 in Brooklyn's Marcy Projects. He appeared on Jaz-O's singles in 1989-1990, toured with Big Daddy Kane in 1994, and sold tapes from his car. After being rejected by every major label, he co-founded Roc-A-Fella Records with Damon Dash and Kareem 'Biggs' Burke in 1995 and released his debut album in 1996.","primary_leverage_engine":"Entrepreneurial self-creation","normalized_primary_engine":"Execution / operations","secondary_engine":"Brooklyn hip-hop ecosystem","started_serious_reps_before_20_score":1,"prior_reps_score":2,"scarce_skill_depth_score":1,"native_distribution_score":1,"elite_ecosystem_network_score":1,"complementary_team_score":2,"structural_wave_score":2,"concentration_intensity_score":1,"capital_safety_score":0,"domain_proximity_score":2,"total_leverage_score":13,"success_tier":1,"leverage_evidence_confidence":"Medium","family_context_summary":"Jay-Z (Shawn Carter) was born in Brooklyn and raised in the Marcy Projects public housing complex. His father abandoned the family when he was young. He grew up in poverty and was involved in drug dealing before pursuing music full-time.","parent_family_domain_summary":"Not documented in reviewed sources.","early_family_financial_platform_support_score":0,"parent_family_domain_advantage_score":0,"inherited_audience_business_network_score":0,"elite_institution_performance_pipeline_score":0,"frontier_geography_ecosystem_score":2,"rare_early_tools_facilities_score":0,"dedicated_mentor_coach_tutor_score":1,"exceptional_peer_cofounder_sibling_score":2,"early_online_platform_community_score":0,"direct_customer_domain_exposure_score":2,"prodigy_physical_edge_score":0,"adversity_constraint_catalyst_score":2,"inherited_access_stack_count":6,"exceptional_inherited_access_count":4,"all_documented_early_condition_count":6,"primary_early_advantage_archetype":"Constraint-driven self-creation","primary_early_advantage_tags":"Brooklyn hip-hop ecosystem, self-founded label, street-level distribution, mentor Jaz-O, Roc-A-Fella co-founders, adversity-driven","evidence_summary":"Jay-Z grew up in the Marcy Projects in Brooklyn and started rapping at 16. He was mentored by Jaz-O and appeared on records in the late 1980s, but was rejected by every major label in New York. In 1995, he co-founded Roc-A-Fella Records with Damon Dash and Kareem 'Biggs' Burke, and released his debut album 'Reasonable Doubt' in June 1996 at age 26, which peaked at #23 on the Billboard 200. His path was defined by adversity—poverty, rejection by labels—and self-creation, leveraging Brooklyn's position as the center of 1990s hip-hop.","early_advantage_evidence_confidence":"High","source_count":4,"primary_source_url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jay-Z","source_urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jay-Z","https://www.ebony.com/reasonable-doubt-at-30-story-behind-jay-z-debut/","https://www.complex.com/music/a/jesse-serwer/jay-zs-best-early-songs","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reasonable_Doubt_(album)"],"annotation_status":"subagent_researched_beta","source_audit_status":"not_independently_audited","data_version":"0.2.0-subagent-beta","eligibility_status":"age_26_eligible"}
