{"person_id":"billy-wright","name":"Billy Wright","cohort_group":"Athletes","category":"Footballer (soccer player)","birth_year":1924,"age_at_milestone":24,"milestone_by_age_26":"Became England football captain in 1948 (age 24) and won the FA Cup with Wolverhampton Wanderers in 1949 (age 25), having been club captain since 1947.","early_history_summary":"Wright joined Wolverhampton Wanderers' ground staff at 14 in 1938, made his senior friendly debut at 15, and accumulated over 100 wartime appearances. He made his official debut in January 1946 (age 21), became club captain around 1947, earned his first England cap in September 1946, and was made England captain in 1948 at age 24.","primary_leverage_engine":"Early specialization in professional football","normalized_primary_engine":"Early specialization / prior reps","secondary_engine":"Elite performance pipeline at Wolves","started_serious_reps_before_20_score":1,"prior_reps_score":2,"scarce_skill_depth_score":1,"native_distribution_score":0,"elite_ecosystem_network_score":1,"complementary_team_score":1,"structural_wave_score":1,"concentration_intensity_score":1,"capital_safety_score":0,"domain_proximity_score":2,"total_leverage_score":10,"success_tier":2,"leverage_evidence_confidence":"Medium","family_context_summary":"Wright was born in Ironbridge, Shropshire, the son of Thomas Wright, a worker at the Coalbrookdale Company ironworks. He was encouraged by a school teacher to respond to a newspaper advertisement for Wolves trials.","parent_family_domain_summary":"Not documented in reviewed sources.","early_family_financial_platform_support_score":0,"parent_family_domain_advantage_score":0,"inherited_audience_business_network_score":0,"elite_institution_performance_pipeline_score":2,"frontier_geography_ecosystem_score":1,"rare_early_tools_facilities_score":1,"dedicated_mentor_coach_tutor_score":1,"exceptional_peer_cofounder_sibling_score":0,"early_online_platform_community_score":0,"direct_customer_domain_exposure_score":1,"prodigy_physical_edge_score":0,"adversity_constraint_catalyst_score":1,"inherited_access_stack_count":6,"exceptional_inherited_access_count":1,"all_documented_early_condition_count":6,"primary_early_advantage_archetype":"Elite performance pipeline","primary_early_advantage_tags":"Wolves ground staff program, early professional football, England captaincy, FA Cup win, Major Buckley mentorship, wartime football","evidence_summary":"Wright joined Wolverhampton Wanderers' ground staff at age 14 in 1938 after being encouraged by his school teacher to attend trials. He made his senior friendly debut at 15 and over 100 wartime appearances before his official debut in January 1946 at age 21. He became Wolves club captain around 1947, earned his first England cap in September 1946, and was made England captain in 1948 at age 24. He led Wolves to FA Cup victory in 1949 at age 25. His early path was built on early entry into the Wolves academy system and rapid progression to club and national captaincy.","early_advantage_evidence_confidence":"High","source_count":4,"primary_source_url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billy_Wright_(footballer,_born_1924)","source_urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billy_Wright_(footballer,_born_1924)","https://www.wolves.co.uk/club/history/hall-of-fame/billy-wright/","https://www.englandfootball.com/england/mens-senior-team/squad/Legends-profiles/billy-wright","https://www.wolves.co.uk/news/features/20240206-billy-wright-cbe-100-years-since-the-birth-of-a-legend/"],"annotation_status":"subagent_researched_beta","source_audit_status":"not_independently_audited","data_version":"0.2.0-subagent-beta","eligibility_status":"age_26_eligible"}
